# Primary workers for zai-org/GLM-5.3 (sglang).
# lib/runtime/src/admission_gate.rs reads this from each worker process; the
# frontend does not read it. `export` so sourcing the file without `set -a`
# still reaches the worker process. Set it on every primary worker.
# sglang reports its engine waiting queue, so the margin is enforceable.
# The value bounds how many requests may sit in the engine's own queue before
# the worker is excluded from selection. Keep it above the policy's failover
# point so the policy decides to spill first.
# 0 is rejected: the runtime reads a present 0 as an always-firing gate.
# Source docs/spillover/tuning.md for the default's derivation.
# See admission/<model>/proxy.env for the proxy opt-out.

export DYN_ADMISSION_QUEUE_MARGIN=256
